From 9fe20f6d33aa52eb78944a3b98b3e3796bf8183e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Junxiao Chang <junxiao.chang@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 14:59:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] drm/i915: disable PMU events on PREEMPT_RT

Running perf with i915 PMU events on PREEMPT_RT kernels can trigger
warnings such as "schedule while atomic" or "BUG: sleeping function
called from invalid context".

The call trace is:

rt_spin_lock+0x63/0x200
i915_pmu_enable+0x48/0x390 [i915]
i915_pmu_event_add+0x71/0x90 [i915]
event_sched_in+0x105/0x270
merge_sched_in+0x2db/0x4e0
perf_event_sched_in+0x83/0xa0
remote_function+0x4f/0x70
__flush_smp_call_function_queue+0xca/0x6e0

Perf events may be scheduled from a CPU different from the target CPU.
In this case, perf uses smp_call_function_single() to execute the event
handler remotely while preemption is disabled.

The i915 PMU event path acquires a spinlock for synchronization.
On PREEMPT_RT kernels, spinlocks become sleeping locks, which can lead
to scheduling from an atomic context and trigger the warnings above.

As a workaround, disable i915 PMU event support when PREEMPT_RT is
enabled.

Signed-off-by: Junxiao Chang <junxiao.chang@intel.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_pmu.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_pmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_pmu.c
index 96392f470cfe..671194d63073 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_pmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/i915/i915_pmu.c
@@ -1164,6 +1164,12 @@ void i915_pmu_register(struct drm_i915_private *i915)
 	};
 	int ret = -ENOMEM;
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT)) {
+		/* Workaround: disable i915 PMU support on PREEMPT_RT kernels */
+		drm_info_once(&i915->drm, "i915 PMU is disabled on PREEMPT_RT kernels\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
 	if (IS_SRIOV_VF(i915)) {
 		drm_info(&i915->drm, "PMU not supported for this GPU.");
 		return;
-- 
2.34.1

